.TITLE "chmod"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes the access permissions of files and directories. It manages who can __read__, __write__, or __execute__ a file using either symbolic or octal modes.

.DIV "TLDR"
**chmod mode file**
Applies specific permissions to a file using numeric or symbolic modes.
> __mode__ numeric (e.g., 755) or symbolic (e.g., +x) | __file__ target file

**chmod +x file**
Makes a file executable for the current user, group, and others.
> __+x__ execute permission

**chmod 644 file**
Sets permissions so the owner can read/write, while others can only read.
> __644__ octal mode (rw-r--r--) | __file__ target file

**chmod -R mode folder**
Changes permissions for a directory and all its contents recursively.
> __-R__ recursive flag | __mode__ permission mode | __folder__ target directory

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using octal modes (like __755__) is often faster for setting exact permissions, while symbolic modes (like __+x__) are better for making quick adjustments. Always use __-R__ with caution to avoid accidentally locking yourself out of critical directories.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:chown** **cli:ls** **cli:umask**

